WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:10.480 --> 00:00:13.340
Good morning, John. It's Thursday, March 8th.

00:00:13.340 --> 00:00:19.820
I'm walking downtown to try and find some people to give peeps to. There are technically a lot of people around

00:00:20.340 --> 00:00:25.040
but they're all in cars. I'm having a hard time getting them to notice me.

00:00:25.040 --> 00:00:26.439
Free peeps!

00:00:26.439 --> 00:00:31.529
Free, free peep-, free, no, I'm not stopping. It's kind of snowing and cold.

00:00:32.250 --> 00:00:34.250
I kind of hate you a lot.

00:00:36.160 --> 00:00:38.800
Starting to be a lot more people around.

00:00:38.920 --> 00:00:41.200
This is the kind of town I live in.

00:00:41.260 --> 00:00:48.060
My general opinion is that it's going to be quite difficult to get rid of these peeps.There are a lot less people downtown than I thought there would be.

00:00:48.060 --> 00:00:50.060
I usually only go downtown at night,

00:00:50.060 --> 00:00:53.320
so I kind of assumed that it would just be a bunch of college students,

00:00:53.320 --> 00:00:55.480
who are kind of mostly drunk.

00:00:55.480 --> 00:01:01.040
But it's not drunk college students. It's business people and soccer moms on errands.

00:01:01.040 --> 00:01:03.300
They don't look like they want peeps.

00:01:03.320 --> 00:01:08.120
Also, I don't know how I'm going to film them because people usually aren't okay with that kind of thing.

00:01:08.129 --> 00:01:10.180
I think I'm gonna have to hide the camera.

00:01:10.180 --> 00:01:13.540
This looks like a pretty good place to hide a camera.

00:01:15.060 --> 00:01:17.060
Want one? Free peeps.

00:01:17.060 --> 00:01:18.760
Man: Can't even give those things away, huh?

00:01:18.760 --> 00:01:20.140
It's very difficult.

00:01:20.360 --> 00:01:24.420
You might want to take some peeps home. They're free.

00:01:27.020 --> 00:01:29.660
Hi, do you like peeps?

00:01:31.500 --> 00:01:32.180
Hi.

00:01:34.120 --> 00:01:35.780
She ran away from me.

00:01:35.860 --> 00:01:38.300
Okay, I just got a bunch.

00:01:39.700 --> 00:01:44.420
[Singing to himself]

00:01:49.220 --> 00:01:50.660
This isn't working.

00:01:51.220 --> 00:01:55.720
Okay, this looks promising. There's a bunch of punk rockers down the street.

00:01:55.840 --> 00:01:58.260
But it's going to be hard to record them.

00:01:58.260 --> 00:02:03.680
So I'm just going to turn the camera on and leave it in my pocket-- you *hear* what happens.

00:02:04.760 --> 00:02:06.460
Hey guys.

00:02:06.460 --> 00:02:08.220
I have a ridiculous number of peeps.

00:02:08.220 --> 00:02:09.660
(Man 1): I would love some peeps.

00:02:09.660 --> 00:02:11.660
I mean, I have like a hundred of them.

00:02:11.660 --> 00:02:14.980
(Man 1): Oh damn, don't competitively eat amongst yourselves.

00:02:14.980 --> 00:02:16.400
[Laughter]

00:02:16.400 --> 00:02:17.120
(Man 1): Definitely.

00:02:17.120 --> 00:02:22.000
I've been trying to give them away all day. People are like [high-pitched] "there's a crazy guy trying to give me peeps"

00:02:22.000 --> 00:02:23.270
[More laughter]

00:02:23.270 --> 00:02:24.040
(Man 1): Nice

00:02:24.040 --> 00:02:27.440
You don't have to take all of them, but I would appreciate it if you did.

00:02:27.440 --> 00:02:29.440
(Man 1): We're going to.

00:02:30.200 --> 00:02:31.740
I'm Hank, by the way.

00:02:32.320 --> 00:02:34.500
(Man: 1) I'm Kurt. (Hank): Hey Kurt.

00:02:34.500 --> 00:02:36.700
(Man 2): I'm Brad. (Hank): Hey. (Brad): Nice to meet you.

00:02:36.700 --> 00:02:40.260
(Man:) Machine Gun. (Hank): Hey, Machine Gun. (Machine Gun): Nice to meet you.

00:02:40.260 --> 00:02:43.220
That's, uh, twelve peeps in your hand right now.

00:02:43.220 --> 00:02:45.020
(Kurt): Yep, twelve peeps.

00:02:45.220 --> 00:02:47.780
I do not want you to choke yourself.

00:02:48.320 --> 00:02:53.300
(Man): No, y'know, he does this for a living. A freakshow. Just watch. Just watch.

00:02:53.800 --> 00:02:58.200
(Man): Focus. (Hank): Seriously, people die eating peeps all the time.

00:03:02.520 --> 00:03:05.300
We should be timing you.

00:03:08.660 --> 00:03:11.380
(Brad): One more man. Put it in there.

00:03:16.460 --> 00:03:19.940
It's amazing how much your dog doesn't care about peeps.

00:03:19.940 --> 00:03:21.600
How you feeling?

00:03:21.680 --> 00:03:28.900
(Kurt): That's a lot of peeps. I feel like I have the Stay Puft Marshmallow Man like fighting the Ghostbusters in my stomach.

00:03:28.900 --> 00:03:30.140
Okay

00:03:30.150 --> 00:03:31.620
See you guys.

00:03:31.620 --> 00:03:32.700
(Man): Definitely.

00:03:32.700 --> 00:03:34.180
Thank you very much.

00:03:34.180 --> 00:03:38.520
Those guys are probably the most worthy recipients of peeps I have ever seen.

00:03:38.520 --> 00:03:44.220
So I went back and timed him and it took him one and a half minutes to do what it took me six minutes to do.

00:03:44.220 --> 00:03:46.900
However, I actually felt really,

00:03:46.920 --> 00:03:48.040
really,

00:03:48.040 --> 00:03:49.580
nauseous at the end of it.

00:03:49.580 --> 00:03:54.040
And I hope Kurt is okay because that was a lot of peeps really fast.

00:03:54.040 --> 00:03:58.240
Anyway, I have to keep this under 4 minutes, so I'll see you tomorrow.

